oox: let a text shape obey TextAutoGrowHeight when it is exported to DOCX (pdf-docx module only).

DrawingML::WriteText writes <a:spAutoFit/> in a DOCX bodyPr only for an SdrObjCustomShape whose TextAutoGrowHeight is
true (tdf#112312: other shapes defaulted the property to true and were wrongly exported as auto-fit), and <a:noAutofit/>
for everything else. The PDF import's text boxes are plain text shapes whose graphic style sets draw:auto-grow-height
and draw:auto-grow-width on purpose (WriterXmlFinalizer::visit(FrameElement)), so they always came out as noAutofit: a
reader that draws a wider font than the PDF's wraps the line and the box keeps its height, which hides the overflow.

In this module every text shape comes from the PDF import, which sets the property deliberately, so here a text shape
obeys it too. The file is named *-pdf-docx.patch, which pipeline/lib/fingerprint.sh sends to the pdf-docx module ONLY;
every other module keeps the tdf#112312 rule. Not observed in Word.

diff --git a/oox/source/export/drawingml.cxx b/oox/source/export/drawingml.cxx
index 7e119c3..6deb9c3 100644
--- a/oox/source/export/drawingml.cxx
+++ b/oox/source/export/drawingml.cxx
@@ -4347,10 +4347,13 @@ void DrawingML::WriteText(const Reference<XInterface>& rXIface, bool bBodyPr, bo
 
         if (GetDocumentType() == DOCUMENT_DOCX || GetDocumentType() == DOCUMENT_XLSX)
         {
-            // tdf#112312: only custom shapes obey the TextAutoGrowHeight option
+            // tdf#112312: only custom shapes obey the TextAutoGrowHeight option.
+            // BUG-43 (pdf-docx module only, see the patch header): every text shape of a PDF import sets it on purpose
+            // (draw:auto-grow-height in the importer's graphic style), so here a text shape obeys it too.
             bool bTextAutoGrowHeight = false;
             auto pSdrObjCustomShape = xShape.is() ? dynamic_cast<SdrObjCustomShape*>(SdrObject::getSdrObjectFromXShape(xShape)) : nullptr;
-            if (pSdrObjCustomShape && GetProperty(rXPropSet, u"TextAutoGrowHeight"_ustr))
+            const bool bTextShape = xShape.is() && SdrObject::getSdrObjectFromXShape(xShape) != nullptr;
+            if ((pSdrObjCustomShape || bTextShape) && GetProperty(rXPropSet, u"TextAutoGrowHeight"_ustr))
             {
                 mAny >>= bTextAutoGrowHeight;
             }
